{
  "name": "ORYVIA",
  "description": "ORYVIA is a local workstation for phenotype-genotype association and posterior-effect candidate review in plant quantitative genetics. It aligns phenotype and genotype matrices, imports tabular and VCF data, and runs GLM and mixed-model association scans, with optional native rMVP FarmCPU. Empirical-Bayes and native multivariate mash workflows estimate adjusted effects and uncertainty while retaining trait units, genotype coding, carrier support and sensitivity information. Reference annotations and dosage-based linkage disequilibrium support interval-to-gene lookup. Manhattan, quantile-quantile, effect-interval and response plots export source data and settings. Users can work through a browser on Windows, macOS or Linux, or run headless batch manifests with verified resume. Slurm and PBS scripts are generated on request without automatic job submission. Synthetic examples and input templates are included.",
